ck_isosceles(a, b, c):\n    return a == b or a == c or b == c\n\nThen, in the solution.py file, this function is defined. The user might also want to make sure that the function is properly formatted with proper spacing and syntax. But since the user mentioned using black or yapf, I should ensure that the code is formatted correctly. However, since the user is just asking for the code, I can present it as is, assuming that the formatting tool will take care of it.\n\nI need to make sure that the function is correctly named and that the parameters are in the right order. The problem states the function takes three integer inputs, so the parameters are a, b, c.\n\nNo other issues here. The problem seems straightforward. The user might have wanted to test if I can write a simple function, but the rules about formatting and versioning are just part of the company's standards, which I need to follow.\n</think>\n\n<answer>\ndef check_isosceles(a, b, c):\n    return a == b or a == c or b == c\n</answer>"
