\n\nWait, but the problem says to return a list containing only the odd integers. So the list comprehension would filter out the even numbers.\n\nYes. That\'s the correct approach.\n\nNow, the code needs to be in a file called solution.py. So the code would be in that file.\n\nSo the answer is the function as described. But I need to make sure that the code adheres to the company\'s coding standards. The filename is correct, the function is named correctly, and the code uses list comprehensions which are valid.\n\nI think that\'s all. The code is simple and meets all the requirements.\n</think>\n\n<answer>\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef Split(mixed_list: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    return [num for num in mixed_list if num % 2 != 0]\n</answer>'
