k like:\n\ndef sum_series(n):\n    total = 0\n    current = n\n    while current > 0:\n        total += current\n        current -= 2\n    return total\n\nBut the problem says the function should handle only positive integers. However, the function doesn't include error checking. But the problem might not require that, so the code will proceed as is.\n\nNow, the user wants the code in a new file named experiments/solution.py. So, I'll write that function in the file.\n\nI need to make sure the function is correctly named and the parameters are correct. The function is supposed to take a single integer n as input.\n\nSo, the final code would be in the solution.py file with that function.\n</think>\n\n<answer>\ndef sum_series(n):\n    total = 0\n    current = n\n    while current > 0:\n        total += current\n        current -= 2\n    return total\n\n# Solution implemented in experiments/solution.py\n</answer>"
